  "question": {
    "text": "The general solution of the differential equation $\\frac{d y}{d x}+\\frac{2}{x} y=x^2$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PdLyA",
      "text": "\n$y=c x^{-3}-\\frac{x^2}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VoXgz",
      "text": "\n$y=c x^3-\\frac{x^2}{4}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ufHF6",
      "text": "\n$y=c x^2+\\frac{x^3}{5}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Q2zxd",
      "text": "\n$y=c x^{-2}+\\frac{x^3}{5}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given differential equation is\n$$\n\\frac{d y}{d x}+\\frac{2}{x} \\cdot y=x^2\n$$\nThis is of the linear form.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore P=\\frac{2}{x}, Q=x^2 \\\\\n& \\text { I.F }=e^{\\int \\frac{2}{x} d x}=e^{\\log x^2}=x^2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nSolution is\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& y \\cdot x^2=\\int x^2 \\cdot x^2 d x+c=\\frac{x^5}{5}+c \\\\\n& y=\\frac{x^3}{5}+c x^{-2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
